[[File:Droid_Repair_Bay_Raddus.png|thumb|300px|The [[Raddus (MC85 Star Cruiser)|''Raddus'']] was a Mon Calamari Star Cruiser.]]
{{Quote|Were you on a star cruiser or a...?|[[Luke Skywalker]]|<ref name="Episode 4">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
A '''Star Cruiser''' was a type of [[cruiser]]. The term was frequently used to refer to [[Mon Calamari]] [[MC-series star cruiser|cruisers]],<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> such as the [[MC75 Star Cruiser|MC75 modified star cruiser]],<ref name="Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> [[MC80 Star Cruiser]],<ref name="SWE Mon Calamari star cruiser">{{SWE|technology|moncalcruiser|Mon Calamari star cruiser}}</ref> and the [[MC85 Star Cruiser]]<ref name="ICS">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref> used by the militaries of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]],<ref name="Episode VI" /> the [[New Republic]],<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> and the [[Resistance]].<ref name="BTA">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref>

==Mon Calamari Star Cruisers==
{{Main|MC-series star cruiser}}
===MC75 Star Cruiser===
The [[MC75 Star Cruiser]] was a type of star cruiser made by the [[Mon Calamari]]. They were originally manufactured as [[city-ship]]s, and were converted into [[warship]]s when the Mon Calamari joined the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="Visual Guide" /> There were at multiple types of MC75 cruisers including; the [[MC75 Armored Cruiser]], the [[MC75 Ordnance Cruiser]],<ref name="Profundity Expansion">{{Armada|set=Profundity Expansion Pack|cardname=Mon Calamari Exodus Fleet}}</ref> the [[MC75B Star Cruiser]] and the [[MC75C Star Cruiser]].<ref name="Ships">{{SWKidsYouTube|series=Star Wars By the Numbers|text=Every Ship in the Star Wars Sequel Trilogy|video=bb3vhWXClTY|nolive=1}}</ref>

===MC80 Star Cruiser===
[[File:MCLiberty.jpg|thumb|229x229px|A [[MC80 Liberty Type Heavy Star Cruiser|''Liberty''-class]] variant of the MC80.]]
The [[MC80 Star Cruiser]]<ref name="Manual">''[[YT-1300 Millennium Falcon Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref> was another type of star cruiser manufactured by the Mon Calamari.<ref name="UltimateSW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> The [[MC80 Liberty Type Heavy Star Cruiser|MC80 ''Liberty'' Type Heavy Star Cruiser]]<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> and the [[MC80A Home One Type Heavy Star Cruiser|MC80A ''Home One'' Type Heavy Star Cruiser]] were variants of the MC80.<ref name="Starfighters">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref>

===MC85 Star Cruiser===
The [[MC85 Star Cruiser]] was the first starship type commissioned by the [[New Republic]] after the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="ICS" />

===MC95 Star Cruiser===
The [[MC95 Star Cruiser]] was a model of starship made by the Mon Calamari. There were multiple variants including the [[MC95A Star Cruiser]], the [[MC95B]] Star Cruiser, the [[MC95C Star Cruiser]], the [[MC95D Star Cruiser]], and the [[MC95E Star Cruiser]].<ref name="Ships" />

===Unidentified Star Cruisers===
The Mon Calamari also made a [[Unidentified Mon Calamari cruiser (Geist)|star cruiser with blunted fins]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars NE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref>

==Other Star Cruisers==
===MPO-1400 Star Cruiser===
The [[MPO-1400 Purgill-class star cruiser|MPO-1400 ''Purgill''-class star cruiser]] was a model of star cruiser that was used by [[Chandrila Star Line]].<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=disney-parks-experiences-and-products-reveals-new-magic-at-d23-expo-2019|text=Disney Parks, Experiences and Products Reveals New Magic at D23 Expo 2019}}</ref>

===Hynestian Star Cruiser===
The [[Hynestian Star Cruiser]] was in use by the [[Citizens' Fleet]] at [[Exegol]].<ref name="Ships" />

